From 1a243cef9d07bcc700565454c8c9b069d3d388d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@localhost>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:05:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ruffle_sdl: pause key, vsync frame pacing, heap trims in
 spare time

* Pause (--pause-key, --pause-with): a key that suspends the player (no
  frames, timers or audio) and draws a banner over the last frame
  ("PAUSED", Start to resume, Select+Start to quit) with scissored clears,
  so no shader and no GL state wgpu relies on. With --pause-with the key
  only becomes the pause key once the movie has loaded a file of that
  name (the Fancy Pants hub, World4/FPAWorld4.swf, has no pause; the other
  worlds have their own on the same key). Keys pressed or released while
  paused are given to the movie on resume (the last event of each), so
  none is left stuck down. Player::shift_start_time takes the pause out of
  getTimer(), so a clock-timed game does not run the pause as one step.
* --frameskip-with: turns on RUFFLE_FRAMESKIP (now also settable at run
  time, Player::set_frameskip) once the movie loads a file of that name,
  so World 3 gets it however it was started.
* Frame pacing (RUFFLE_PACING=0 turns it off, RUFFLE_REFRESH_HZ sets the
  refresh rate when SDL does not know it): a 30 fps movie on a 60 Hz
  screen was shown one refresh after its tick when it drew in under a
  refresh and two refreshes after when it took longer, so frames stayed
  on screen for one, two or three refreshes in turn, and the clock
  drifting against the screen moved frames between refreshes every few
  seconds. A frame is now held until the refresh before its slot has
  passed, the next tick runs right after the swap, and a tick's time step
  within 15% of whole movie frames is rounded to them. Pacing turns itself
  off when swaps do not wait for the refresh.
* malloc_trim ran on the main thread every 2 s whatever the frame was
  doing. It now runs in time the frame has to spare (before the frame's
  slot, or before the next frame is due, or while paused), sized by what
  the last trim took, and at the latest every 16 s.
* Two malloc arenas (mallopt M_ARENA_MAX, unless MALLOC_ARENA_MAX is set).
